Scope of the Reference Implementation

This release includes:

• structural transition definitions
• path validity rules
• minimal executable reference (visual path demo)
• outputs and reference traces

STRAL-Path defines a deterministic structural model where path correctness emerges from structure:

resolve(structure) ->

RESOLVED   if structure_mature and exactly one valid path exists
ABSTAIN    if structure is incomplete
CONFLICT   if multiple valid paths exist or structure is inconsistent

What This Demonstrates

• path correctness without traversal
• independence from graph search (BFS / DFS)
• independence from ordered exploration
• transition correctness does not require traversal
• structural maturity governing path visibility
• safe handling of incomplete or conflicting structure
• deterministic and reproducible transition outcomes
• identical structure produces identical visible state and certificate

Conformance

An implementation is considered compatible if it preserves:

• structure-based correctness
• independence from traversal as a requirement
• deterministic resolution
• structural maturity-driven visibility
• reproducibility of visible state and certificate under equivalent inputs
• explicit handling of incomplete and conflicting structure

Conformance is judged solely by observable behavior — not by internal implementation.

S1 = S2 -> VisibleState1 = VisibleState2 -> Certificate1 = Certificate2

Conflict Handling

In this reference implementation:

• CONFLICT is explicitly defined and demonstrated
• ABSTAIN behavior corresponds to incomplete structure (no visible path)
• invalid or inconsistent paths do not influence the visible state

Conformance requires:

• no forced path under incomplete structure
• no arbitrary selection under conflicting structure

Canonical Transition Identity (Forward Path)

Extended implementations may include canonical identity:

canonical(resolve(S)) -> transition_identity

This enables:

• equivalence across different valid path structures
• normalization of transition truth
• identity independent of representation

This is not required for the reference implementation.

Relationship to Shunyaya Framework

STRAL-Path is part of the broader Shunyaya framework.

It builds on:

• SLANG → structural resolution without execution
• ORL → order-independent correctness
• STINT → correctness without connectivity
• STIC → correctness without cloud dependency
• STRAL → transition without space-time primitives

